# ============================================================================
# FlowAblation / 1D contact of a gas and a conducting solid  (Hydro2, ablation.conduction = 1)
#
# Check of the in-depth conduction of the embedded solid and of the fluid|solid thermal
# coupling, with NO ablation (ablation temperature out of reach).  Gas at rest (rho 1, p 1,
# cp 3.5 -> T = 1; k_g = mu cp/Pr = 4.861e-3, alpha_g = 1.389e-3) fills x > 0.5; the solid
# (rho_s 1, cp_s 14, k_s 1.944e-2 -> alpha_s = alpha_g, effusivity e_s = sqrt(k rho c) = 4 e_g)
# starts at T_s0 = 0.99.  Two half-spaces in contact:
#   surface temperature (constant)  T_i = (e_g T_g + e_s T_s0)/(e_g + e_s) = 0.992
#   each side  T = T_i + (T_far - T_i) erf(|x - 0.5| / (2 sqrt(alpha t)))
# The 1 % temperature difference keeps the gas density change (neglected in the exact
# solution) small.  Measured (400 cells, t = 5): T_i +0.02 % of dT, profiles 0.17 % (gas),
# 0.02 % (solid) of dT.
#
# Run (from bin/): mpirun -np 4 ./hydro2-2d-g++ ../tests/FlowAblation/input_1D_Contact plot_file=<dir>/output
# Check:           python3 ../tests/FlowAblation/reference/solid_conduction_check.py contact <dir>
# ============================================================================
plot_file = ./tests/FlowAblation/output_1D_Contact
